WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.880
My parents ask me to read small print. Suniye turns a shared image or P D F into Hindi speech, with large controls.

2
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:16.960
This image is cropped from a real public electricity notice. Share the picture to Suniye. Text recognition happens on the phone.

3
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:26.400
O C R can make mistakes. This page needs a separate confirmation. The app speaks a warning first. Flagged number groups are withheld.

4
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:56.433
Hindi audio: an OCR caution, then the notice about contacting the consumer grievance forum. The recognized source stays visible.

5
00:00:56.433 --> 00:01:07.233
Now a complete two page Hindi notice, with paragraphs, dates, and numbers. Suniye reads one page at a time. These are excerpts from completed playback checks.

6
00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:30.233
Page 1 begins with the OCR caution and the notice heading. The full page completed playback in the recorded test.

7
00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:40.567
The next page has its own review. Repeat replays the recording. Slow reduces its speed. Stop stays below the scrolling text.

8
00:01:40.567 --> 00:02:00.567
A later excerpt from page 2. Flagged number groups are spoken as “unclear number”; OCR can still make mistakes.

9
00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:11.700
In WhatsApp, open the image or P D F. Choose Share, then Suniye. For a text message, use Share if available, or copy it into Suniye.

10
00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:19.940
English explanations for this walkthrough. Hindi controls and reading in the app. Every voice you hear is ElevenLabs Raju.
